# Game scene / match

## Ownership

- Orchestration: `game.gd` applies `GameConfig` via `ResourceUtils.update_resource`
- Live `game_config.tres` on the scene = standalone defaults
- States: `GameManager` FSM only (`Serve` / `Play` / `Point` / `MatchEnd`)
- Features: `blob_player`, `ball`, `ai_opponent`, `virtual_controls` — scene wires and reacts to `ev_*`

## Change guide

| Goal | Touch |
|------|--------|
| Round / match transitions | FSM states + `FSMGameEvents` |
| Scoring / 3-touch fault | `MatchController` + `PointState` |
| Player feel | `src/features/blob_player/` |
| Ball physics | `src/features/ball/` |
| Bot | `src/features/ai_opponent/` |
| Touch / virtual stick | `src/features/virtual_controls/` — left half move (`p1_left/right`), right half jump (`p1_jump`) |
| HUD | `ui/` — listen to `GameEvents` |

## Constraints

- Exit match via `root_events.ev_exit_game` with post-battle payload
- `vs_ai` / `max_touches` come from `GameConfig`, not hardcoded
- Prefer small `RefCounted` helpers over growing states
- More than `max_touches` (default 3) on one side → fault, opponent scores
- No dual-touch local 2P: both halves are **P1 only** (left = move, right = jump); P2 uses keyboard (`p2_*`)
